itive","claim_refs":["sha256:f22708f3180068944c06829213f78f6ecfb65ef34f6c8decded774b95a041d92/nodes/scalar.smooth_positive_density"],"content_span":{"end_byte":171688,"end_line":3791,"start_byte":169329,"start_line":3747},"evidence_class":"source_argument","query_href":"/api/v1/papers/query?manifest=22326593cd4ee37735df71d5e7612efdc02bf148d61a9361dc2d26629a464dbf&paper=long&passage=density-positive&representation=matches","reading_href":"/api/v1/papers/reading?manifest=22326593cd4ee37735df71d5e7612efdc02bf148d61a9361dc2d26629a464dbf&paper=long&passage=density-positive","ref":"sha256:4c6350e9b4de8b6fa8cb1160f0ada57e4a2b797aebd0c518c88b1ace1b27878b/papers/long.md/sha256:8c370b67aa0a6f2b705479e8d6814e78733322389d75881ba1c79f94458dfa9b/papers/long.json/passages/density-positive","section_ref":"sha256:4c6350e9b4de8b6fa8cb1160f0ada57e4a2b797aebd0c518c88b1ace1b27878b/papers/long.md/sections/165299","section_title":"9. Density and finite-disorder consequences","stage":"long","treatments":[{"claim_id":"scalar.smooth_positive_density","claim_ref":"sha256:f22708f3180068944c06829213f78f6ecfb65ef34f6c8decded774b95a041d92/nodes/scalar.smooth_positive_density","kinds":["derivation","application"],"rationale":"Applies the shared fixed-time spatial estimate after smoothness and moment saturation. Its proof destination records the nonminimizing artificial plateaus and fixed-strip transfer."}]},{"anchor":"density-consequence","claim_refs":["sha256:f22708f3180068944c06829213f78f6ecfb65ef34f6c8decded774b95a041d92/nodes/scalar.smooth_positive_density","sha256:f22708f3180068944c06829213f78f6ecfb65ef34f6c8decded774b95a041d92/nodes/support.fixed_time_spatial_coercivity"],"content_span":{"end_byte":41367,"end_line":915,"start_byte":33928,"start_line":744},"evidence_class":"source_argument","query_href":"/api/v1/papers/query?manifest=22326593cd4ee37735df71d5e7612efdc02bf148d61a9361dc2d26629a464dbf&paper=short&passage=density-consequence&representation=matches","reading_href":"/api/v1/papers/reading?manifest=22326593cd4ee37735df71d5e7612efdc02bf148d61a9361dc2d26629a464dbf&paper=short&passage=density-consequence","ref":"sha256:0cd16e6afa4096fccc55a516a798b7287a6570a5e77248099820f99b2079800b/papers/short.md/sha256:2ffc265585cd63413034841fe74b99bdfd311b903d8e1690214debca0c3a94c0/papers/short.json/passages/density-consequence","section_ref":"sha256:0cd16e6afa4096fccc55a516a798b7287a6570a5e77248099820f99b2079800b/papers/short.md/sections/33815","section_title":"4. The coercive inequality at a fixed time and positivity of the density","stage":"short","treatments":[{"claim_id":"scalar.smooth_positive_density","claim_ref":"sha256:f22708f3180068944c06829213f78f6ecfb65ef34f6c8decded774b95a041d92/nodes/scalar.smooth_positive_density","kinds":["derivation"],"rationale":"Develops smoothness from the quotient of moments before differentiating, then transfers the quantitative spatial-moment inequality through local constant replacements at a fixed interior time. Compact-strip stability is a cited input; positivity is asserted only for 0<t<1, and the argument does not transfer third time derivatives or add formal acceptance."},{"claim_id":"support.fixed_time_spatial_coercivity","claim_ref":"sha256:f22708f3180068944c06829213f78f6ecfb65ef34f6c8decded774b95a041d92/nodes/support.fixed_time_spatial_coercivity","kinds":["derivation","explanation"],"rationale":"Derives the continuous-coefficient fixed-time inequality by admissible local constant replacement and common-strip convergence of spatial moments, then applies it after q=t. Minimality is unnecessary for the transfer itself."}]},{"anchor":"density-and-approximation","claim_refs":["sha256:f22708f3180068944c06829213f78f6ecfb65ef34f6c8decded774b95a041d92/nodes/scalar.smooth_positive_density"],"content_span":{"end_byte":60759,"end_line":1431,"start_byte":60020,"start_line":1422},"evidence_class":"source_argument","query_href":"/api/v1/papers/query?manifest=22326593cd4ee37735df71d5e7612efdc02bf148d61a9361dc2d26629a464dbf&pap